   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">A quaternary notation system for accounting for transactions with financial instruments developed</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">According to the recommendations presented in the 2008 SNA, a financial account is a flow table that should reflect transactions on the exchange of financial assets between sectors of the economy and the rest of the world, as well as corresponding records related to the movement of financial assets during the acquisition and disposal of non-financial assets. This approach determines the reflection of transactions from two balance sheets - from the balance sheet of the recipient of the financial instrument, and from the balance sheet of the seller (issuer, etc.) of this financial instrument.</narrative>
    </description>
