   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The methodology of the SNA balance of assets and liabilities through gender lenses developed.</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Development of a methodology for the balance of assets and liabilities of the SNA, which in turn will act in an integrated sequence of accounts as a consolidating tool for the initial and final stocks of financial and non-financial assets available in the economy, as well as for the flows associated with these assets. A balance sheet is a report compiled at a certain point in time containing data on the value of assets owned by an institutional unit or group of institutional units and the value of liabilities assumed by an institutional unit or group of institutional units.</narrative>
    </description>
